  data: {
    LLM: "Always play to foundations as soon as possible - there's no reason to delay. This is the primary rule of Carpet.\n\nUse empty carpet spaces strategically to hold dealt cards you can play soon. Try to create chains of same-suit cards in the carpet so they can cascade to foundations.\n\nPlan several moves ahead. Create same-suit sequences in the carpet (e.g., 4-5-6-7-8 of Spades) so when the 4 goes to foundation, the rest follow quickly. Keep high cards in discard until foundations are built up close to their level, or until you have free carpet space.",
